oken connection. That means one short log line with the request dump, the error added to `c.Errors`, and the request aborted.\n- **Test:** I added `TestPanicWithAbortHandler` to `recovery_test.go`. Before the fix it failed because the server returned a 500 and logged a stack trace. After the fix it passes. I also removed the fix temporarily and confirmed the test fails again without it.\n- **Checks:** `go test ./...` passes in every package, and `go vet` and `gofmt` are clean. The diff is 27 added lines across those two files.\n- **Visible behaviour change:** recovery functions passed to `CustomRecovery` are no longer called for this panic, which matches how broken pipes already work. This is the main thing to know before merging.\n- **Not done:**\n  - I didn't re-panic so Go's HTTP server handles the abort itself (silently dropping the connection). That would be closer to what `net/http` intends, but every middleware further up the chain would see the panic, so it's a bigger change.\n  - Nothing is committed yet. Say if you want it committed under `fix(recover): suppress http.ErrAbortHandler in recover`.","ttft_ms":3290,"type":"result","duration_ms":37633,"uuid":"dfb89437-bce0-41b7-af07-9876be65658c","ttft_stream_ms":3288,"time_to_request_ms":156,"first_content_frame_ms":3289,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
